  "worked_solution": "To evaluate, we substitute $t=0$ into the function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{(0)+1} \\\\ 1-(0)^{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}\u2061(0)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{1} \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the value of $f(t)$ at $t=0$ is $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$",
